---
title: Installing the Game
tableOfContents: true
---
You can download the game by going to our [GitHub](https://github.com/p3d-project/persona-3-dual) & clicking the latest release

{% SizedImage
   src="/docs/imgs/install-game/github.png"
   alt="GitHub Downloads"
   width=800 /%}

Currently, we only support:

- [**melonDS Desktop**](https://melonds.kuribo64.net/downloads.php) (Windows/Linux/MacOS)
- [**melonDS Android**](https://github.com/SapphireRhodonite/melonDS-android/releases) (Android)
- **Console (DS / DSi / 3DS)** via [TWiLight Menu++](https://wiki.ds-homebrew.com/twilightmenu/)

> Other versions of melonDS may work, but are untested.

> Other flashcard launchers may work, but are untested.

### melonDS (Desktop)

[Watch the YouTube tutorial](https://youtu.be/ZjzYzYCTrNI)

1. Download `persona-3-dual.nds` and `sdcard.img.zip` from the latest release, & decompress `sdcard.img.zip`
1. In melonDS, go to **Settings → DLDI** and enable DLDI.
1. Set the SD card image path to the generated `sdcard.img`.

> **Do NOT enable "Sync SD card to folder"**. This will wipe the contents of the folder!

Now, you can open melonDS and load the `persona-3-dual.nds` ROM!

{% SizedImage
   src="/docs/imgs/install-game/melonds.png"
   alt="melonDS"
   width=316 /%}

### melonDS (Android)

[Watch the YouTube tutorial](https://youtu.be/M2TUw532Mzs)

> Android support is experimental. Some odd behaviour may occur throughout your gameplay.

> Ensure that you use `melonDualDS v0.7.0.rc3 Hotfix 2` or newer.

1. Download `persona-3-dual.nds` and `data.zip` from the latest release, & decompress `data.zip`
1. In melonDS, go to **Settings → System** and disable JIT (`Enable JIT` should be unchecked).
1. In melonDS, go to **Settings → System** and enable `DLDI / Homebrew SD`. Then, set the SD folder to your extracted `data` folder.

Now, you can open melonDS and load the `persona-3-dual.nds` ROM!

> **NOTE**: It will take a little bit of time to load into the main menu

### Console (DS / DSi / 3DS)

> Ensure you have the **latest version** of [TWiLight Menu++](https://wiki.ds-homebrew.com/twilightmenu/).

1. Download `persona-3-dual.nds` and `data.zip` from the latest release, & decompress `data.zip`

1. On your SD card, navigate to your `/roms/nds/` folder (or equivalent).

1. Copy `persona-3-dual.nds` and the entire `/data` folder into that directory:

   ```
   /roms/nds/
   ├── persona-3-dual.nds
   └── data/
       ├── music/
       ├── video/
       └── ...
   ```

1. **TWiLight Menu++ on flashcart (R4-type gamecard)**: In  settings, ensure

- **DLDI access** is set to **ARM9**
- **Game Loader** is set to **nds-bootstrap**

> If you don't see these options, navigate between different settings pages using L/R. These should already be the default options.

5. **TWiLight Menu++ on firmware (DSi/3DS)**: In settings, ensure

- TWiLight Menu++ is set to run in DSi mode

6. Launch the game through TWiLight Menu++ as normal.

*Example of correct settings for step 4, TWiLight Menu++ on flashcart (R4-type gamecard)*

{% SizedImage src="/docs/imgs/install-game/dldi.jpg" alt="DLDI" width=400 /%}

{% SizedImage
   src="/docs/imgs/install-game/bootstrap.jpg"
   alt="Bootstrap"
   width=400 /%}

## FAQs

### Do you support melonDS on Android?

We have **experimental** Android support. See [above](guides/install-game/#melonds-android) for more details.

### (melonDS) Launching the game results in a white screen!

Ensure that you have `JIT` turned off in settings (`Enable JIT` should be unchecked).

### (Console) I've launched the game on my game console & have gotten a save error!

We've noticed that Windows will sometimes decompress the data.zip folder into *another* data folder.

```
data/
 └── data/
     ├── music
     ├── environments
     ├── ...
```

This is incorrect! Make sure you only have **one data folder**

```
data/
 ├── music
 ├── environments
 ├── ...
```

Also, make sure you are running the latest version of TWiLight Menu++ & have set the correct settings

### (DSi/3DS) I cannot find DLDI settings!

DLDI settings are only on flashcarts (R4-type game cards) running TWiLight Menu++. See [above](/guides/install-game/#console-ds--dsi--3ds) for more details.
